On Mon, Nov 26, 2001 at 05:55:58PM +0000, Alan Cox wrote:
>=20
> > Can anybody tell me if "NCR3580.c" needs a bit of "standardisation" and=
 imp=3D
> > rovment, particularely, does it need to support SCSI 2 ITLQ nexuses wit=
h TA=3D
> > GGING support!?
>=20
> There are several 5380.c variant drivers that are much cleaner - the ARM
> stuff is nice, there is also the m68k/mac 5380 driver which has scsi-2 in=
 it
>=20
> The driver works for me (non SMP) as is, but Im sure 2.5 wil finally break
> it properly.
>

Thanks for this reply.

After your advice,
I have tried to replace NCR5380.c by mac_NCR5380.c on my PC, with the kerne=
l 2.4.17 when I started last year!=20
I go very slowly because I only mess around with SCSI bus software after da=
rk and before going to rest, it helps difficult digestion.

after lots of try and fail I compiled a version which seems to be not crash=
ing with only a scanner attached to it.

I have to say it is not a glorious one, but in the process I think, I resol=
ved a hanging problem which would happen with the original kernel and the N=
CR5380.c compiled with it.=20
I might be boosting a bit too early, but I think it is worth to report thes=
e suspicions which might have been addressed in the kernel 2.5 series.

It looked that for some reasons, I have not yet grasped, sometimes,=20
when aborting a command they are NULL fields in the Scsi_Cmnd structure,
and L2/L3 drivers are not enjoying the prospect of it!=20
So in scsi_old_done(), scsi_done(), sg_cmd_done_bh(), I put more checks on =
occurrences of references of NULL pointers.
see L2/L3 the attached patch for those changes.
These would sweep the problems under the carpet...


Now, I have not tested the fixes, but by doing a dozen of scanning with my =
200Mhz heavy loaded donkey, it stood still for a few hours.... but never cr=
ashed.=20
What a lovely feeling.

Could you spare a few fraction of seconds of expert eyes and check if those=
 patches have a meaning.


I have also attached a big patch file for using mac_NCR5380.c with g_NCR538=
0.c, just for reference of course!

In this system I have refined a bit the IRQ lock time around the manipulati=
on of Scsi_Cmnd queues.
In the process I might have removed some locks when time on the device is c=
ritical...oops.
I messed around the debugging comments.
Have not checked yet all the DMA transfer part (nor TAG part...).
Well it is just for information really but somebody might find some interes=
t (who knows?).=20
I have found mine: I am a step closer to enjoy mad scanning (after dark).


Anyway, after all this,=20
I still do not understand what is so good about SCSI bus, than other type o=
f bus?=20
I might miss a big point.
Also, at what point SG drivers request synchronious data transfer? Will tho=
se freeze the PC if it happens?

=20
Cheers,

Christian.





